│   ✅ Agent Finished                                                                              │
│                                                                                                  │
│   Message:                                                                                       │
│     I fixed `Segment.split_cells` in `rich/segment.py` so it no longer returns a left part wider │
│ than the cut when the text contains zero-width or combining characters. The patch is submitted   │
│ (one file, 480 bytes).                                                                           │
│                                                                                                  │
│     The cause was in `_split_cells`: its proportional estimate for the split position could land │
│ past the cut when the prefix was already wider than the requested cell count. The forward scan   │
│ then never walked back. I added a loop that rewinds the position while the prefix is wider than  │
│ the cut.                                                                                         │
│                                                                                                  │
│     I checked the fix with an exhaustive brute-force run over short strings mixing ASCII, wide   │
│ CJK, emoji, combining marks and zero-width spaces. Before the fix there were 256 width           │
│ violations; after it there are none. `tests/test_segment.py` passes (52 tests). I did not add a  │
│ regression test, and I did not check the exact Textual scenario from the linked issue.           │
